<title>USA: USDA finds more karnal bunt spores in two states.</title>
<headline>USDA finds more karnal bunt spores in two states.</headline>
<dateline>WASHINGTON 1996-11-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>An ongoing national survey detected teliospores of the karnal bunt fungus in 15 additional counties in Alabama and Tennessee, the U.S. Agriculture Department said Tuesday.</p>
<p>USDA said it would &quot;continue to take those administrative and regulatory actions necessary to conduct the full range of appropriate containment and eradication measures.&quot;</p>
<p>In Alabama, the teliospores were found in Lauderdale, Jackson, DeKalb, Cherokee, Lee, Autauga, Baldwin, Escambia and Tuscaloosa counties. In Tennessee, they were found in Lawrence, Cumberland, Grundy, Clayborne, Marshall and White counties.</p>
</text>
